    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Brief and settings\nThe Form Trigger collects the brief, tone, sender name, optional subject, attachment mode, optional file, the Google Sheet URL and a Test mode switch. \"Settings\" cleans these values and holds the daily cap (default 200). Edit dailyCap there.",
        "height": 224,
        "width": 160,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "83fc125a-f091-4e32-9c60-e5adfe5ccdfe",
      "name": "Note: Brief and settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        128
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Read and clean contacts\nReads every row (columns: name, email, status, attachment_file; add sent_at and error columns for logging). Skips empty or invalid emails, duplicates and rows already \"sent\". Test mode keeps only the first 3. Contacts past the daily cap (minus rows already sent today) become \"pending\".",
        "height": 224,
        "width": 384,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "b3637231-3e4a-4a9c-989c-330de9bf0906",
      "name": "Note: Read contacts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        464,
        128
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. AI draft and approval\nClaude writes ONE email with a {{name}} placeholder (runs once, not per contact). You get it by email with Approve / Reject + feedback. Rejections go back to the AI, up to 3 redrafts. Nothing is sent before you approve.",
        "height": 304,
        "width": 1088,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "0d2e7084-212b-41c6-963a-104ee774872e",
      "name": "Note: Draft and approval",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        768,
        128
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Queue approved contacts\nAttaches the approved subject and body to each contact. Contacts over the daily cap are marked \"pending\" in the sheet and not sent.",
        "height": 352,
        "width": 992,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "9c8b1462-de79-4ba7-9a4e-b4ff3d374cf9",
      "name": "Note: Queue contacts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1280,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5. Personalize, attach and send\nLoops one contact at a time. Replaces {{name}} (or \"there\" if empty), builds HTML plus a plain-text fallback, adds the attachment per mode (uploaded file, or the Drive file named in attachment_file; missing file = skipped and logged), sends over SMTP, then logs sent/failed with timestamp and error to the sheet. A random 5-15 second pause follows each contact. A failed send does not stop the run.",
        "height": 640,
        "width": 2320,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "a8cd5b9b-e273-407a-a623-309e4264eaf9",
      "name": "Note: Send loop",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1520,
        64
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 6. Run summary\nWhen the loop ends, emails you totals: sent, failed, skipped and pending.",
        "height": 224,
        "width": 384,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "09bf1ec1-1ac9-42ad-b897-db08a3d0d5cb",
      "name": "Note: Summary",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2048,
        32
      ]
    }
